msgid "Optimization using Servers"
msgstr "Optimización usando Servidores"

msgid "There is an extra layer of complexity."
msgstr "Existe una capa extra de complejidad."

msgid "Performance is lower than when using simple APIs directly."
msgstr "El rendimiento es menor que al utilizar APIs simples directamente."

msgid "More memory is needed."
msgstr "Se necesita más memoria."

msgid "Still, Godot is designed to work around this problem."
msgstr "Aún así, Godot está diseñado para solucionar este problema."

msgid ""
"You can see how using low-level servers works in action using the `Bullet "
"Shower demo project <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/"
"master/2d/bullet_shower>`__."
msgstr ""
"Puede ver cómo funciona el uso de servidores de bajo nivel en acción "
"utilizando el `proyecto de demostración Bullet Shower <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/bullet_shower>`__."

msgid "Servers"
msgstr "Servidores"

msgid "RIDs"
msgstr "RIDs*"

msgid ""
"The key to using servers is understanding Resource ID (:ref:`RID "
"<class_RID>`) objects. These are opaque handles to the server "
"implementation. They are allocated and freed manually. Almost every function "
"in the servers requires RIDs to access the actual resource."
msgstr ""
"La clave para utilizar los servidores es comprender los objetos Resource ID "
"(:ref:`RID <class_RID>`). Estos son identificadores opacos para la "
"implementación del servidor. Se asignan y liberan manualmente. Casi todas "
"las funciones de los servidores requieren RIDs para acceder al recurso real."

msgid ""
"Most Godot nodes and resources contain these RIDs from the servers "
"internally, and they can be obtained with different functions. In fact, "
"anything that inherits :ref:`Resource <class_Resource>` can be directly "
"casted to an RID. Not all resources contain an RID, though: in such cases, "
"the RID will be empty. The resource can then be passed to server APIs as an "
"RID."
msgstr ""
"La mayoría de los nodos y recursos de Godot contienen estos RIDs de los "
"servidores de forma interna, y se pueden obtener mediante diferentes "
"funciones. De hecho, cualquier cosa que herede de :ref:`Resource "
"<class_Resource>` se puede convertir directamente a un RID. Sin embargo, no "
"todos los recursos contienen un RID; en esos casos, el RID estará vacío. El "
"recurso luego se puede pasar a las APIs de los servidores como un RID."

msgid "For nodes, there are many functions available:"
msgstr "Para los nodos, hay muchas funciones disponibles:"

msgid ""
"For CanvasItem, the :ref:`CanvasItem.get_canvas_item() "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_canvas_item>` method will return the canvas "
"item RID in the server."
msgstr ""
"Para CanvasItem, el método :ref:`CanvasItem.get_canvas_item() "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_canvas_item>` retornará el RID del canvas item "
"en el servidor."

msgid ""
"For CanvasLayer, the :ref:`CanvasLayer.get_canvas() "
"<class_CanvasLayer_method_get_canvas>` method will return the canvas RID in "
"the server."
msgstr ""
"Para CanvasLayer, el método :ref:`CanvasLayer.get_canvas() "
"<class_CanvasLayer_method_get_canvas>` devolverá el RID del lienzo en el "
"servidor."

msgid ""
"For Viewport, the :ref:`Viewport.get_viewport_rid() "
"<class_Viewport_method_get_viewport_rid>` method will return the viewport "
"RID in the server."
msgstr ""
"Para Viewport, el método :ref:`Viewport.get_viewport_rid() "
"<class_Viewport_method_get_viewport_rid>` devolverá el RID del viewport en "
"el servidor."

msgid ""
"Try exploring the nodes and resources you are familiar with and find the "
"functions to obtain the server *RIDs*."
msgstr ""
"Intenta explorar los nodos y recursos con los que estás familiarizado y "
"encuentra las funciones para obtener los *RIDs* del servidor."

msgid ""
"It is not advised to control RIDs from objects that already have a node "
"associated. Instead, server functions should always be used for creating and "
"controlling new ones and interacting with the existing ones."
msgstr ""
"No se recomienda controlar los RIDs de objetos que ya tienen un nodo "
"asociado. En cambio, las funciones del servidor siempre deben usarse para "
"crear y controlar nuevas e interactuar con las existentes."

